{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-zariski}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b6fb7b7a543c466e47420c8b4a8ba5b9ed0e8d3644729f144c3d95fd83fde94", "source_text": "The Zariski topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc55721a3be8a2b9484fb7529bc21758b5f1ee427ed00318a24e3f95dd7c0cfc", "unit_id": "tag:020N:title"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T = \\bigcup f_i(T_i)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-zariski-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283f9dea2be6a5f99e7e729bc3db42e6c914a1813f97c1b0e20c1ac32623e25a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b55b04160fde668857e3d1f9d22681daaf68075c3461ed8e81ae26c0f097d41", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Zariski covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is an open immersion and such\nthat <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9efbb1c6f289bd2f5d550a16a18dcaeed4c9728f843a02406eacef0a462110f2", "unit_id": "tag:020O:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be7fc1a1a4b3934a2549317fc6d38c20a64f91e846d7ddfe06f61a457fa4bfb4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis defines a (proper) class of coverings.\nNext, we show that this notion satisfies the conditions of\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6127c5022e28f66a4645eeb831f4c83e36bdee2bbda4843c612fce9fdf6976d6", "unit_id": "tag:020N:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:56f057b720fc00be1aa3343e0bfc55e0a8a7b66685e26173cf1a3bfd6081a137", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis a Zariski covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a Zariski covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have a Zariski covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is a Zariski covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is a Zariski covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is a Zariski covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5690f65e8abb4c702e6844de3eb92033e36dcc1d6ecabdcb61846091803dac05", "unit_id": "tag:020P:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:792a4dd319050af03f893ecf120848a7a734812b94394fe6c78a241052b02fe4", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:020P:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_j$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$U_j$", "MATH_0009": "$T_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-standard-covering}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5a29d032233e10ca4aae4418cebc2d436970539706abf5069d808bca0e39f03a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4453ebde615ffa3535c82f289fff4afc4a0057f95ed8c6b202b96482647a2d61", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a\nZariski covering of <MATH_0003>. Then there exists a Zariski covering\n<MATH_0004> which is a refinement\nof <MATH_0005> such that each <MATH_0006> is a standard\nopen of <MATH_0007>, see\nSchemes, Definition <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, we may choose each <MATH_0008> to be an open of one of the <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be2dab4963c001c637ac63442a858b6374fcac1f3c39230a4063bed5f28b4980", "unit_id": "tag:020Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "020N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-standard-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:77dc6e1af9e07fd811c8cf6c01db1ffca2ef23ecb357e720061ef8ff8a05de90", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:054d766725c687a4f66167f21f43eb20263f5b19c0665f14ef1225474f465cdf", "source_text": "Follows as <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact and standard opens form a basis\nfor its topology. This is also proved in\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a2ccccffa978b769ae10b0739285f41b01db6ef1f15988878951073ea70522e0", "unit_id": "tag:020Q:proof"}
